From f66f5ce7a630170ec67267f93e4ae23ac42e28aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:23:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] CUDA: PTQ1_0 decode surgery for consumer Ada/Ampere
 (Bonsai 2 27B, +18% TG)

Same weights, same 1.75 bpw, bit-identical GEMV math (test-backend-ops MUL_MAT
78/78 and MUL_MAT_ID 75/75 vs CPU; greedy generations identical). Measured on an
RTX 4070 12 GB: 50.9 -> 60.1 tok/s TG128 at stock clocks.

1. quantize_q8_1<exact_isum>: store the exact int16 sum of the 32 q8 values in
   ds.y for PTQ1 consumers. The vec-dot accumulates raw trits {0,1,2} with DP4A
   and subtracts the bias once per block, deleting __vsub4 (no native SIMD byte
   subtract on sm_89) from every 4-weight round. TG flat, power 192 -> 179 W.

2. Warp-transposed (SoA) q8 activation layout (ggml_cuda_ptq1_q8_word). In the
   small-K geometry each lane owns a K-block and read 36 activation words from
   block_q8_1 structs 144 B apart per lane: ~36 L1 lines / ~1300 wavefronts per
   K-iteration for activations vs ~250 for the weights, capping the GEMV at
   ~370 GB/s. K-blocks are grouped by 32 and word w of the group stored
   contiguously, so the same load is one wavefront. Same bytes per column.

3. Warp-per-row small_k geometry in mul_mat_vec_q for PTQ1: the stock small_k
   loop strides K-blocks across the whole block (kbx = tid; kbx += 128) so for
   K=5120 only threads 0..39 load; warps 2..3 just hold SM slots. Warp w now owns
   row row0+w, lanes stride its K-blocks, shuffle reduction, no shared memory.
   qkv 391 -> 445 GB/s, lm_head 414 -> 460 (CUPTI, in-graph).

4. Fold the recurrent-state GET_ROWS into the GatedDeltaNet kernel
   (ggml_cuda_try_gdn_gather_skip): the kernel indexes cache + ids[seq]*stride
   directly. Removes an 8 us kernel and 3 MB of dirty L2 per GDN layer that was
   being written back in the middle of the FFN weight stream.
   GGML_CUDA_GDN_GATHER_FUSION=0 restores the gather.

Diagnostics (all env-gated, off by default): GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_DUMP,
GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING, GGML_CUDA_GRAPH_STATS, GGML_CUDA_L2_PERSIST.

Method, measurements and the CUPTI injection profiler used to find these are in
https://github.com/professorpalmer/bonsai-ada-surgery
